# The Human Is the Loop
Planning and Shipping Code with Claude Code and GitHub
11 Aug 2026

Petar Djukic
meshintelligence.substack.com

## Overview

- Everyone says "loop engineering": replace yourself as the person who prompts the agent
- I'm responsible for what ships, so I stay in control
- Loop engineering is a set of tools and a set of skills — the four skills I show you live today:
  - **[getting the model to write its own prompts](https://meshintelligence.substack.com/p/how-to-loop-engineering)** — the push command
  - **[long-term memory management](https://meshintelligence.substack.com/p/how-to-use-github-as-long-term-memory)** — GitHub as the agent's memory
  - **[giving every task its own workspace](https://meshintelligence.substack.com/p/how-to-use-git-worktrees-with-coding)** — worktrees and the pop command
  - **[giving the agent temporal agency](https://meshintelligence.substack.com/p/how-to-use-github-to-give-a-coding)** — recurring issues
- The talk summarizes [my blog](https://meshintelligence.substack.com) — every skill has a write-up

.html qr-overview.html

: Set expectations: live demo on a real repo, things may flake, that is part of the point. The tools — four commands, GitHub, markdown files, no framework — get named on the loop slide, so say that out loud here rather than reading it. Each skill maps to one demo beat and one article.

